r the Seventh Congress of Soviets)","Artist":"El Lissitzky","Date":"Published 1935","Medium":"Seven volumes: six bound (vols. 1–6) and one folder of maps (vol. 7). Each bound volume with gravure, lithograph, collotype, and relief-halftone reproductions, primarily of photographs, with additional reproductions of drawings, paintings, graphs, diagrams, and other images, printed in black, colored, and metallic inks on paper; letterpress text; leaves in various sizes, some with foldout flaps, accordion folds, transparentized paper, or die-cut holes. Publisher’s original side-sewn bindings (vols. 1–6), each with paper cover, lithographed title in red and metallic ink, embossed illustration, and red or tan cloth spine. One lithographed folder (vol. 7) containing two lithographed maps and a saddle-stitched letterpress-printed pamphlet. Publisher’s original box: tan cloth over board with reproduction of a photograph by Anatoly Skurikhin (The Builders of Kuznetsk, c. 1930–31), printed title, and metallic foil-stamped design; interior with flaps of paper and board with red and tan cloth, printing, and embossing","CreditLine":"Gift of Helen and Sam Zell","URL":"https://www.moma.org/collection/works/434547","ImageURL":"https://www.moma.org/media/W1siZiIsIjY0MjQyNiJdLFsicCIsImNvbnZlcnQiLCItcmVzaXplIDEwMjR4MTAyNFx1MDAzZSJdXQ.jpg?sha=f8e984b8fb0f9025"},{"ObjectID":447469,"Title":"Miami Silver from Arles/Miami","Artist":"Malcolm Morley","Date":"1973","Medium":"One from a portfolio of five lithographs and colophon page","CreditLine":"Gift of Dr. Samuel Mandel","URL":"https://www.moma.org/collection/works/447469","ImageURL":"https://www.moma.org/media/W1siZiIsIjU0MjM1NiJdLFsicCIsImNvbnZlcnQiLCItcmVzaXplIDEwMjR4MTAyNFx1MDAzZSJdXQ.jpg?sha=aecd7e1c32ff4bba"}]